{"id":"fd12767d-23cd-4541-b202-bdbf0f437782","expr":"result.getClass() == c || result.getClass().getSuperclass() == c","rationale":"Often the instantiated object's class is either c or a direct subclass if a subclass instance is returned, but this depends on the implementation and can vary.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.badlogic.gdx.utils.reflect.ClassReflection#newInstance(Class<T>):T","file":"com/badlogic/gdx/utils/reflect/ClassReflection.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T17:05:34.961939246Z"}
{"id":"cff35ac8-7847-4689-bcdc-a1d7f589220c","expr":"result == null || result.getDeclaringClass() == c","rationale":"Invariant that if result is non-null, then its declaring class is the input Class c.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.badlogic.gdx.utils.reflect.ClassReflection#getConstructor(Class,Class):Constructor","file":"com/badlogic/gdx/utils/reflect/ClassReflection.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T17:05:35.211545200Z"}
